  == page 11 ==
Heads of Household
Male headed household recorded 61.9 percent slightly down from 63.2 percent registered in the
2001 Census. Female headed households moved from 36.8 percent in 2001 to 38.1 in 2011(Table
4). Children within households recorded 23,637 or 34.1 percent of the population in comparison
to 24,589 or 35.21 percent in 2001. The total number of households moved from 22,733 in 2001
to 25,113 in 2011 registering a 10.5 percent increase.
Ethnicity
The ethnic composition of the population remains predominantly of Afro descent recording 84.8
percent (Table 5.1). However steady decreases have been registered as this group has declined by
4.9 over 1991. Other groups have recorded steady increases with Kalinago increasing to 3.7
percent from 2.4 percent in 1991 and 2.9 in 2001. White/Caucasians accounted for 1.3 percent
from 0.8 percent in 2001 while Mixed group accounted for 8.7 percent slightly decreasing from
8.9 percent in 2001.
Religion
Roman Catholics accounted for 52.7 percent of the population. This religion has registered
steady decreases over the last decades from 70.1 percent in 1991 down to 52.7 percent in
2011(Table 6.1). On the other hand, Evangelicals have grown 12.1 percent over the last decade
representing 19.0 percent of the population. Seventh Day Adventist recorded a 10.6 percent
increase representing 6.7 percent of the population. Interestingly, persons with no religious
beliefs significantly increased by 54.4 percent moving from 6.1 to 9.4 percent of the population.
